---------------------------------------------------------------------

New features for MiNT 0.8:

	-- the code for working around the dLibs argv[] bug has been
removed, because it was interfering with programs that used
base->p_parent to see if they were started as a .PRG or .ACC. Sorry,
but if I have to break programs I'd rather break the programs that were
obviously doing something illegal. Alas, this means lots of Sozobon
compiled programs break -- the fix is to get Sozobon (a nice compiler),
fix the library, and recompile.

	-- file handles -2 and -3 are now supported, and may be redirected
just like CON:, e.g. Fforce(-2, Fcreate("FOO", 0)) sends all printer output
to the file "FOO"

	-- data may be read from/written to process address spaces using the
pseudo-files on drive X:

	-- new TT GEMDOS calls (Mxalloc, etc.) are now supported,
as are the concepts of "fast ram" and the various loader bits. Of course,
if you don't have any fast ram in your computer this won't matter much.

	-- improved minix filesystem support, including support for
floppy disks and removable hard drives

	-- the mouse driver now updates the line A mouse variables, so
that MGR and similar programs will work with large screen emulators

	-- signal handling has been integrated with normal exceptions,
so that e.g. a bus error raises the SIGBUS signal. A side effect is 
that instead of getting two bombs for a bus error, you get a message
like "pid 4: BUS ERROR". You may or may not find this more useful.
